          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Ehrenfeucht-Fraïssé games
            are a technique in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            for studying whether two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures+in+model+theory"} structures
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+equivalence"} elementary equivalent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+logic"} first-order logic
          %p
            The games are played by two players: the
            = succeed "," do
              %em spoiler
            = succeed "," do
              %em duplicator
          %p
            A game is played in turns for a number of rounds (in general an ordinal, but usually a finite number or
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
