            %h6#example Example
            %p Any two algebraically closed fields of equal characteristic and infinite transcendence degree over their respective prime subfields are back-and-forth equivalent. A back-and-forth system is in this case given by the pairs of generating sequences for isomorphic finitely generated subfields.
          #ThmCountableBF.num_example
